# No em dashes in copy

Never use the em dash character (`—`, U+2014) in anything a person reads in the product or in AI replies to the user.

**Covers:** UI labels, helper text, errors, toasts, empty states, aria-labels, metadata descriptions, emails, and chat responses.

**Prefer instead:** a comma, a period and a new sentence, parentheses, or a colon.

```text
❌ Missing bio — won’t appear in the directory.
✅ Missing bio. Won’t appear in the directory.
✅ Missing bio, so it won’t appear in the directory.

❌ Account menu — profile needs attention
✅ Account menu: profile needs attention
```

Code comments and internal docs may keep em dashes. User-facing strings must not.
